%N A400105 Decimal expansion of Sum_{m>=2} (-1)^m / log(m*(m+1)/2).
%C A400105 The series converges by the Leibniz criterion, since 1/log(m*(m+1)/2) decreases monotonically to 0 for m >= 2, but it converges only conditionally and extremely slowly: the error after truncating at m is asymptotic to 1/(4*log(m)), so direct summation is not a practical method of evaluation. The integral representation in the Formula field converges geometrically.
%H A400105 Gnouma Jerome Kadouno, <a href="/A400105/b400105.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..999</a>
%F A400105 Equals Integral_{t=0..oo} A(t) dt, where A(t) = Sum_{m>=2} (-1)^m * (m*(m+1)/2)^(-t). This follows from 1/log(x) = Integral_{t=0..oo} x^(-t) dt, valid since T_m >= 3 for m >= 2, together with dominated convergence.
%F A400105 A(t) -> 1/2 as t -> 0+ (Abel summation of 1 - 1 + 1 - ...) and A(t) ~ 3^(-t) as t -> oo, so the integral converges at both ends.
%F A400105 A(n) at positive integers n is the sequence whose coordinates in the basis {1, log(2), zeta(3), zeta(5), ...} form the triangle A399988; in particular A(1) = 3 - 4*log(2) = 4*A239354.
%e A400105 0.589597759773905767773781169332680698570462681563930403592982116261553959...
%o A400105 (PARI)
%o A400105 \p 120
%o A400105 sumalt(m=2, (-1)^m/log(m*(m+1)/2))
%o A400105 (PARI)
%o A400105 \p 60
%o A400105 A(t) = sumalt(m=2, (-1)^m*(m*(m+1)/2)^(-t));
%o A400105 intnum(t=0, [+oo, log(3)], A(t))
%Y A400105 Cf. A399988, A239354, A000217.
%K A400105 nonn,cons,new
%O A400105 0,1
%A A400105 _Gnouma Jerome Kadouno_, Sep 18 2026
